MT7668 DKMS package
===================

Install the headers matching the target kernel before installing this package.
Both wlan_mt76x8_sdio and bt_mt7668 are built from source by DKMS. No prebuilt
modules, firmware, device-tree changes, modprobe configuration or modules-load
configuration are installed. Module loading and board configuration remain under
the administrator's control. Package upgrades do not forcibly unload drivers.

Firmware, including mt7668_patch_e*_hdr.bin for the vendor Bluetooth driver,
must be supplied by the distribution or board image. The in-tree btmtksdio driver and bt_mt7668
must not bind to the same Bluetooth function; choose the driver before loading.

Use scripts/build-deb.sh in a clean, committed Git checkout to build a package.
It derives the package and DKMS version from the commit's UTC timestamp and
12-character SHA, exporting the committed source without changing the checkout.
A direct dpkg-buildpackage uses the checked-in changelog version instead.

Git tags must exactly match scripts/version.sh output. The GitHub workflow
builds artifacts for branches and pull requests and creates a draft release
for an existing matching tag. It does not create or push tags.
